 3187: 
 3188: ## 7. The project rules the questions apply -- quoted with their bounds
 3189: 
 3190: *Quoted from the WORKING-TREE carrier `GXEMUL-SEC/tools/CLAUDE.md` (byte-identical to the root `CLAUDE.md`; 4104
 3191: lines; HEAD's copy has 3846 and lacks the 2026-10-09 clause-(c) block and rule D2).  Line numbers are that file's.*
 3192: 
 3193: **R1 -- THE FLOOR:**
 3194: ~~~~
 3195:  1328| > **THE FLOOR.** A detector is VACUOUS - replace it IN-ROUND - unless it (a) fails on the
 3196:  1329| > pre-fix build, (b) fails on a **VERBATIM REINSTATEMENT of the removed defect at EVERY fixed
 3197:  1330| > site**, and (c) fails on a **NULL MEDIUM** -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under
 3198:  1331| > test (the clause-(c) block below says what that is per instrument kind). Below the floor, the
 3199:  1332| > round's own claim to have "shipped a detector with the fix" is a WRONG RECORD, which the
 3200:  1333| > stopping rule already fixes in-round.
 3201: ~~~~
 3202: **R2 -- clause (c): the null medium, the pre-fix build, the two record forms, and when a claimed clause is L4:**
 3203: ~~~~
 3204:  1340| > **ONE criterion -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under test -- and its object
 3205:  1341| > differs by instrument kind:**
 3206:  1342| > * an offline differential that `#include`s the product: a COMMENT-ONLY product source, which must
 3207:  1343| >   fail to COMPILE, with a gate that reds on the compile failure (measured for `#488`:
 3208:  1344| >   `regress/artifacts/shortread/nullmedium_20261009/RECEIPT.txt`);
 3209:  1345| > * a runtime probe: an ABSENT or NON-EMULATOR binary (every session dies), or a build WITHOUT the
 3210:  1346| >   device for a device round;
 3211:  1347| > * an instruction-handler round: an IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- the
 3212:  1348| >   recommended default, two measured legs at `#527`.
 3213:  1349| >
 3214:  1350| > **THE PRE-FIX BUILD IS CLAUSE (a)'S MEDIUM AND NEVER CLAUSE (c)'S.**  It carries every behaviour of the
 3215:  1351| > product, one of them wrong, so a detector can red on it and still pass a comment-only file -- `#446`,
 3216:  1352| > the instance that created this clause.  A table that wrote "null medium" over a pre-fix leg carries a
 3217:  1353| > WRONG RECORD (L4: correct it in place, quoting what it refutes, as
 3218:  1354| > `ppcrldimimask/killtable_20260911/SCORES.txt` does), NOT a floor breach: clause (c) is then
 3219:  1355| > UNMEASURED there.  **A breach is a genuine null medium coming back GREEN, and nothing else** -- "a
 3220:  1356| > sharper medium was available" is not a floor criterion (at most clause-(e) debt).
 3221:  1357| >
 3222:  1358| > **RECORD CLAUSE (c) IN ONE OF EXACTLY TWO FORMS, never as a bare clause letter beside a row name:**
 3223:  1359| > * `(c): measured at <artifact>` -- the leg was run and its receipt is durable;
 3224:  1360| > * `(c): by construction via <row/pin>, leg not run` -- e.g. the gate pins the row count by EQUALITY
 3225:  1361| >   and a named row reds on a dead run, or the differential `#include`s the product and its gate reds
 3226:  1362| >   on a compile failure.  **A by-construction claim is checked by READING that shape; where the reading
 3227:  1363| >   fails -- no runtime gate wiring, no pin, `check_min`, a control computed over the row list
 3228:  1364| >   (`all([])` is True) -- the leg is OWED** (7n-1's two: the unwired `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` and
 3229:  1365| >   `alpha_tbi_probe.py`).  Predict a dead run's score from the source, not from the row count (Astra
 3230:  1366| >   measured luna's at 0/14 with four gate checks red, and SGI's at 6/46 because six rows test only
 3231:  1367| >   exit status).
 3232:  1368| >
 3233:  1369| > **A claimed-but-unmeasured floor clause is L4 exactly when the record asserts a MEASUREMENT or a
 3234:  1370| > NUMBER that was not made** (`#488`'s "pinned at 90": no preserved 90-row output exists, and the
 3235:  1371| > differential pins 98).  The E1 `[IDENTITY]` self-count row is detector hygiene, NOT clause (c).
 3236: ~~~~
 3237: **R3 -- clause (d), and R4 -- its two shapes:**
 3238: ~~~~
 3239:  1376| > **(d) The detector must also fail when the fix is PRESENT but its REPAIR IS NULLED -
 3240:  1377| > the guard kept, its effect removed.**
 3241:  1428| > **The two shapes, once the enumeration is right:**
 3242:  1429| > * **fix ADDS a predicate** -> weaken the added one (unchanged; the original rule).
 3243:  1430| > * **fix adds none** -> the (d) mutant reroutes an EXISTING guard's repair. For a
 3244:  1431| >   de-fatalisation: **swap the guard's operand for a field the guarded BODY reads.**
 3245:  1432| >   For a pure deletion: **re-introduce the removed behaviour under a DIFFERENT predicate**
 3246:  1433| >   -- not the same one widened, which is (b) wearing (d)'s clothes.
 3247: ~~~~
 3248: **R5 -- the DEPENDS-ON bound:**
 3249: ~~~~
 3250:  1448| > > **DEPENDS ON enumerates exactly two things: (1) the predicates DOMINATING the diff's
 3251:  1449| > > edited lines, walked up only to the ENCLOSING FUNCTION BOUNDARY -- never into callees
 3252:  1450| > > or callers; and (2) for operand-swap forms, swaps drawn ONLY from fields the guarded
 3253:  1451| > > BODY reads (the guard-field/body-field grep the pre-table check already mandates).**
 3254: ~~~~
 3255: **R6 -- joint cells: the body-tested partition:**
 3256: ~~~~
 3257:  1464| > > **DEPENDS-ON enumerates JOINT cells over the guard's operands and the body-read lvalues EXACTLY
 3258:  1465| > > WHEN THE GUARDED BODY'S OWN CODE DISTINGUISHES THEM.**  For each lvalue take the PARTITION the
 3259:  1466| > > body's own tests induce (`pending > 0` gives {0, >0}; `relative_addr == PCCTWO_T1ICR` gives
 3260:  1467| > > {T1, T2}); the enumerated cells are the CROSS-PRODUCT of those partitions -- never arbitrary
 3261:  1468| > > boolean functions of the read-set.  A mutant exempting a single cell whose reachability is
 3262:  1469| > > MEASURED is a floor breach; close the whole cross-product in ONE diff and write into the
 3263:  1470| > > contract which cells are rowed.  A value or combination the body never tests as a case
 3264:  1471| > > (`idata == k`; a byte no conditional distinguishes; both counts >= 2 where the body tests `> 0`)
 3265:  1472| > > is DISCLOSED under clause (e).
 3266: ~~~~
 3267: **R7 -- the floor (cells a row is OWED for) versus clause-(e) disclosure:**
 3268: ~~~~
 3269:  1517| > > **The rule ENUMERATES joint cells wherever the body distinguishes them; the FLOOR -- the cells a row
 3270:  1518| > > is OWED for -- is the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the device-STATE lvalues
 3271:  1519| > > the fix's own repair path reads that are JOINTLY REACHABLE through its own data flow.**  The bits of
 3272:  1520| > > the single value being written are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor; joint cells outside the floor
 3273:  1521| > > are clause-(e) coverage debt, subject to the one ask-again.  A filter may reject or discharge a cell
 3274:  1522| > > but may demand a new row only for a floor cell -- so it cannot grow unbounded.
 3275: ~~~~
 3276: **R8 -- rule D2: a relational compare is pinned at its edges:**
 3277: ~~~~
 3278:  1557| > > For a relational compare against a constant bound B that a fix DEPENDS ON (`X > B`, `e < 96`), each region of its
 3279:  1558| > > generating set is discharged by the row that varies under the LEAST-OBSERVABLE non-equivalent move of B: **X = B+1
 3280:  1559| > > for the region past the bound and X = B-1 for the region below it** (the "at" member is dead where the branch maps B
 3281:  1560| > > to itself).  **A far row proves the branch EXISTS and discharges the BRANCH partition; it never pins the BOUND.**
 3282:  1561| > > Measured on `#473`'s shipped WDC detector: its rows at 68928 and 4998 let `> 32769` and `> 32766` at each clamp --
 3283:  1562| > > one-token bound moves -- pass all 128 rows, while rows at 32769 and 32767 red each one
 3284:  1563| > > (`regress/artifacts/wdc473floor/pass1_20261009/fable5_meas/`).  **Bound: at most two rows per compare the fix
 3285:  1564| > > depends on -- the compare's own two edges.**  It adds no axis; it moves the rows a region already owes to where the
 3286:  1565| > > bound is observable, so it cannot become `#392`.  It is the accept-row finding -- *a single accept row pins exactly
 3287:  1566| > > ONE bound, the one it is near* -- stated for compares.
 3288: ~~~~
 3289: **R9 -- GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD, and the CHANNEL line:**
 3290: ~~~~
 3291:  1740| > | **GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD** | list fields the PREDICATE reads and fields the guarded BODY reads; where they differ, grep whether they are written at the same sites. If not, the detector owes a state where they DISAGREE.  **Also record, per lvalue, the PARTITION THE BODY INDUCES on it** (its tested masks and compare regions) -- EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED is read off this column, never asserted (7n-5, 2026-10-09) | the guard's operand swapped for a field whose third state no row built |
 3292:  1741| > | **CHANNEL** | for each row, name **the mutant it kills** and **the observable that differs under that mutant**. A row whose named channel cannot vary under its named mutant is VACUOUS BY CONSTRUCTION, and that is knowable at writing time, before any table runs | a survival oracle at a REFUSAL-EFFECT site: guarded and unguarded code both survive |
 3293: ~~~~
 3294: **R10 -- a filter cannot demand a row, and R10b -- clause (e), the contract:**
 3295: ~~~~
 3296:  1783| > > **A FILTER CAN REJECT OR REPAIR A ROW; IT CAN NEVER DEMAND A NEW ONE -- SO IT CANNOT GROW
 3297:  1784| > > WITHOUT BOUND.**  That is the stop condition, and it is structural rather than a cap: the
 3298:  1801| > **(e) THE CONTRACT.** The probe header names which edits this detector is designed
 3299:  1802| > to catch. *A detector that says so is falsifiable; one claiming completeness is
 3300:  1803| > not* -- and a later escape becomes "outside the contract" or "a breach of it",
 3301:  1804| > which are different dispositions, rather than an argument about overclaiming.
 3302:  1805| > Two lines in a header.
 3303: ~~~~
 3304: **R11 -- the anchor rule and its reviewer check:**
 3305: ~~~~
 3306:  1814| > **Rows that assert only PAIRWISE DISTINCTNESS, or a same-path round-trip, test the decode
 3307:  1815| > against ITSELF.** They are therefore invariant under any edit that re-maps addresses
 3308:  1816| > INJECTIVELY over the probed set -- translations first among them -- and they catch a re-map
 3309:  1817| > only where it COLLIDES on that set.
 3310:  1888| > **A DETECTOR CLAIMING TO PIN *WHERE* AN ACCESS LANDS MUST CARRY AT LEAST ONE ANCHORED ROW:
 3311:  1889| > > an oracle tied to a SPECIFIC CELL by a channel OUTSIDE the decode under test** -- a side
 3312:  1890| > > effect (a tick that zeroes the cell), an architectural reset value, or a second access path
 3313:  1891| > > to the same cell. **One anchored row converts a whole distinctness suite from relative to
 3314:  1892| > > absolute.**
 3315:  1893| >
 3316:  1894| > **THE REVIEWER CHECK, and it costs two seconds** -- it belongs beside *"does this diff delete
 3317:  1895| > `exit(` from a device? then look for accept rows"*:
 3318:  1896| >
 3319:  1897| > > ***"If every address in this device shifted one word, which row reds?"*** If the answer is
 3320:  1898| > > NONE, position is unpinned, whatever the row count.
 3321: ~~~~
 3322: **R13 -- the addition licence:**
 3323: ~~~~
 3324:  2334| > > **Additions to product code in a hardening fork are licensed by MEASURED DELTAS or by a
 3325:  2335| > > TRANSFERRED WARRANT -- never by "it cannot hurt."**
 3326: ~~~~
 3327: **R14 -- the witness clauses:**
 3328: ~~~~
 3329:  2788| **A rung-2-4 witness is INVALID unless all of:** (i) it shows the defect symptom on the pre-fix
 3330:  2789| committed HEAD and goes green post-fix with the same script - this is test-first itself, restated

